{"qid":"Q203817","names":["First Bulgarian Empire"],"title":"First Bulgarian Empire","endonym":{"native":"Първo българско царство","lang":"bg"},"capsule":"The First Bulgarian Empire was founded around 681 CE when Khan Asparuh led a Bulgar federation across the Danube, defeated Byzantine forces at the Battle of Ongal, and secured Byzantine recognition of a Bulgarian state in the northeastern Balkans. Under Krum (r. 803–814) the empire expanded dramatically, destroyed a Byzantine army and killed Emperor Nicephorus I at the Battle of Pliska in 811, and briefly threatened Constantinople itself. Simeon I (r. 893–927), who converted Bulgaria to Orthodox Christianity and proclaimed himself Tsar, brought the empire to its greatest territorial extent, encompassing most of the Balkans. Byzantine military pressure under Basil II culminated in the annihilation of the Bulgarian army at the Battle of Kleidion in 1014—where Basil blinded some 15,000 prisoners—and the annexation of Bulgaria as a Byzantine province by 1018.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Territorial extent is reconstructed from Byzantine chronicles, Bulgarian inscriptions, and archaeological evidence; frontier zones fluctuated considerably across the empire's three centuries and are modeled with moderate confidence.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: First Bulgarian Empire","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/First-Bulgarian-Empire"},{"label":"Wikipedia: First Bulgarian Empire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Bulgarian_Empire"}],"britannica":"place/First-Bulgarian-empire","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"First Bulgarian Empire",